  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $2x-y\\ge 3?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y & \\ge 3 \\\\ -y & \\ge -2x+3 \\\\ y & \\le 2x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=2x-3.$ Since the inequality involves a 'less than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=2x-3$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a solid line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y\\le 2x-3$ refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line $y=2x-3,$ so we shade *below* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/020b2d81ed5913dfe41fb296811da30ee2c6ea4fc7ea8184335db6d866598c5a.png)",
